# Line endings, fixed per file so a checkout on either OS runs: the sh
# launcher must stay LF on a Windows checkout with autocrlf, and cmd.exe
# misreads a batch file with LF-only endings in places (labels, blocks), so
# the shim is CRLF everywhere. PowerShell reads both; CRLF keeps Notepad happy.
dojo     text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.cmd    text eol=crlf
*.ps1    text eol=crlf
